  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0 (branch cut from upstream/main f490458a).\n\n## What changed\n- New `crates/sim/src/verify/upright.rs`: one predicate, `is_upright`, with one named tolerance `UPRIGHT_TILT_RAD = 1e-9` rad (~5.7e-8 deg). A pose within it is judged exactly as a vertical move (the prismatic branch, bit for bit); above it, downward, sideways, zero or non-finite reads tilted (the enclosing reading).\n- Every verify law that branched on the exact `camcraft_cl::is_vertical` now reads `is_upright`: reach (c) and its mid-turn sweep (c3), fixture bands/rapids (c2)/(d2), posed steel, mesh steel, solid law, posed contact, posed-rapid second reading, all-air verdict.\n- `camcraft_cl::is_vertical` itself stays exact, so CL dumps, posted G-code and goldens do not move.\n- Law (c) no longer reports the same `ShankHit` twice for one move when both band groups (shank and holder) convict with the same verdict.\n- Why 1e-9 rad is safe: at that tilt a 1 m stack moves 1e-6 mm sideways and a 100 mm holder disc dips 1e-7 mm, four orders below a 0.01 mm gouge tolerance. #938's 1e-10 deg (1.7e-12 rad) is three orders inside; a commanded 0.001 deg is four orders outside. The reasoning and the options I dropped are in `docs/decisions/938-tilt-tolerance.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- New `crates/sim/tests/tilt_tolerance.rs` (5 tests; 4 fail on upstream/main without the fix):\n  - `a_wide_holder_reads_the_same_upright_and_at_a_rounding_error_of_tilt`: no pose, [0,0,1] and 1e-10 deg give the same clean verdict (before the fix, 1e-10 deg gave two false ShankHits).\n  - `a_tilt_just_above_the_tolerance_is_still_judged_tilted`: 1.01e-9 rad and 0.001 deg still convict.\n  - `a_noise_tilt_keeps_the_upright_conviction_exactly`\n  - `a_leaning_shank_and_holder_report_one_shank_hit_per_move`\n  - `the_fixture_band_law_reads_noise_as_upright_and_a_real_tilt_as_tilted` (law c2)\n- Unit test `verify::upright::tests::rounding_noise_is_upright_and_a_real_tilt_is_not`, covering both sides plus down, sideways, zero, NaN and inf.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (sim, motion and app suites from the gate map). Also `posed_fixture` and `stock_posed` pass, and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n- One existing expectation changed: `tool_body_bands::a_raised_foot_over_a_fat_shank_is_judged_stricter_than_the_cylinder` had pinned the duplicate `[ShankHit{1,true}, ShankHit{1,true}]`. It now expects a single report. The conviction is the same. No goldens or snapshots moved.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Batch and release tiers were not run, so the heavy `--ignored` lanes did not run.\n- `stock_sim` and the motion generators keep their exact upright tests (they shape geometry, not verdicts). I left them alone on purpose; see the decision file.\n\nChangelog: The verifier treats a tool tilted by rounding noise (up to 1e-9 rad) as upright, so a holder wider than the cutter no longer raises a false collision on float noise, and a move reports a shank/holder hit once (#938)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #938\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
